5. SECURITY, AUTHENTICATION & ROLE-BASED ACCESS CONTROL (RBAC)
================================================================================
5.1. Stateless Firebase Bearer Authentication & Dev-Mock Profile Safeguards:
- Client transmits Firebase ID token in Authorization: Bearer <token> or secure HttpOnly cookie.
- Production Security Lockdown: FirebaseTokenVerifier strictly disables mock auth fallback when the prod profile is active. Any attempt to use mock tokens in production throws an immediate 401 Unauthorized.
- Suspended Account Lockdown: FirebaseAuthFilter immediately rejects deactivated or soft-deleted user accounts with HTTP 403 Forbidden.

5.2. Industry-Standard 2FA / TOTP (RFC 6238 / RFC 4226):
- 160-bit Base32 secret generation using cryptographically secure PRNG.
- Standard otpauth://totp/OpenMosque:<email>?secret=... URI compatible with Google Authenticator, Microsoft Authenticator, and Authy.
- Time-drift tolerance: Validates +/- 1 window (30-second window drift tolerance).
- Single-use backup recovery codes: 8 alphanumeric codes generated and stored exclusively as salted SHA-256 hashes. Consumed codes are permanently deleted on use.
- Step-Up Authentication: Disabling 2FA or regenerating backup codes strictly requires a fresh, valid 6-digit TOTP code or backup code.

5.3. Custom @CurrentUser Parameter Resolver:
- Controllers inject the authenticated User JPA entity directly via @CurrentUser User user.

5.4. User Role Hierarchy & Privilege Escalation Defenses:
- Neutralized Role Escalation: Automatically granting SUPER_ADMIN based on email domains has been permanently eradicated. All newly provisioned users strictly default to UserRole.USER.
- USER: Regular worshipper (search, review, bookmark, propose mosques).
- MOSQUE_ADMIN: Verified Imam/Trustee with verified ownership of their specific mosque.
- MODERATOR: Community Trustee (review crowdsource queue, resolve flags).
- SUPER_ADMIN: System Administrator (manage claims, assign roles, view audit logs).

5.5. Self-Approval & Conflict of Interest Prevention:
- ModerationService prohibits moderators from approving or resolving their own crowdsourced mosque submissions.
- MosqueClaimService prohibits claimants from reviewing or approving their own mosque administration claims.

5.6. Media Security, Magic-Byte Inspection & Path Traversal Mitigations:
- Real header byte inspection (FileSecurityValidator) enforcing valid signatures:
  - JPEG: FF D8 FF
  - PNG: 89 50 4E 47 0D 0A 1A 0A
  - WebP: RIFF....WEBP
  - PDF: %PDF
- Rejection of Windows PE (MZ), Linux ELF, and Java bytecode executables.
- Path Traversal and Null-Byte stripping on all uploaded filenames.

5.7. Strict Multi-Tier Token Bucket Rate Limiting:
- Strict Tier (15 req/min): /api/v1/auth/2fa/**, /api/v1/auth/session, /api/v1/users/sync, media uploads.
- Standard Tier (60 req/min): User contributions, reviews, Q&A submissions.
- Public Read Tier (120 req/min): Mosque directory, prayer times, search queries.

5.8. Production Security Headers & CORS Lockdown:
- Strict-Transport-Security (HSTS): max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains.
- Content-Security-Policy (CSP): default-src 'self'.
- X-Frame-Options: DENY, X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff, Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin.
- Wildcard CORS Credentials Forbidden: Rejects Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * when credentials are true in production.

================================================================================
6. POSTGIS GEOSPATIAL ENGINE & SPATIAL QUERY ARCHITECTURE
================================================================================
6.1. Geometry Representation:
- Coordinates stored as PostGIS geometry(Point, 4326), mapped to LocationTech JTS Point.
- GIST index ensures sub-millisecond execution: CREATE INDEX idx_mosques_location ON mosques USING GIST (location);

6.2. Spatial Proximity Search (ST_DWithin):
SELECT m.*, 
       ST_DistanceSphere(m.location, ST_SetSRID(ST_MakePoint(:lng, :lat), 4326)) / 1000.0 AS distance_km
FROM mosques m
WHERE m.status = 'ACTIVE'
  AND ST_DWithin(
        m.location::geography, 
        ST_SetSRID(ST_MakePoint(:lng, :lat), 4326)::geography, 
        :radiusMeters
      )
ORDER BY distance_km ASC;

